{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_df8c9dc010716c964ed4f93450758d6594bdcc39b23ec7c3d8f4971d3578e797", "title": "Prater", "text": "The Prater (] ) is a large public park in Vienna's 2nd district (Leopoldstadt ). The Wurstelprater amusement park, often simply called \"Prater\", lies in one corner of the Wiener Prater and includes the Wiener Riesenrad Ferris wheel.", "score": 29.4846}, {"id": "hp_doc_5bf5b501feb0c239c72749361fcacf118ed0b3e46a35638fe0020b10a8089546", "title": "Wiener Riesenrad", "text": "The Wiener Riesenrad (German for Vienna Giant Wheel), or Riesenrad, is a 64.75 m tall Ferris wheel at the entrance of the Prater amusement park in Leopoldstadt, the 2nd district of Austria's capital Vienna. It is one of Vienna's most popular tourist attractions, and symbolises the district as well as the city for many people. Constructed in 1897, it was the world's tallest extant Ferris wheel from 1920 until 1985.", "score": 25.4448}, {"id": "hp_doc_3179bc219248db73062968c9ab6568c3ffe7627ee6129f75e87a458d6f3f785c", "title": "Steiger Ferris Wheel", "text": "The Steiger Ferris Wheel is a 60 m tall transportable Ferris wheel. It began operating in 1980, and at that time was the world's tallest transportable wheel, a record documented in the Guinness Book of Records. The world's tallest transportable wheel today is the 78 m Bussink Design R80XL.", "score": 21.0727}], "remaining_searches": 2}
